<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oireachtas</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Oireachtas Éireann</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Oireachtas is the national parliament of Ireland, made up of the President and two houses, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dail-eireann">Dáil Éireann</a> and Seanad Éireann. It was established under the Constitution of 1937, following the parliament of the Irish Free State. The Dáil, elected by proportional representation, chooses the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taoiseach">Taoiseach</a> and is the more powerful chamber.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oireachtas.jpg" alt="Oireachtas" width="320" height="281" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lough Swilly · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:34th_D%C3%A1il_Seating_Plan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
